  characterName: "Aim\xE9e Lumumba (CEO)"
  promptText: My supply chain sources cobalt tied to child labour and conflict. Continuing
    sales meets shareholder demands and sustains jobs; halting production disrupts
    incomes but severs ties to exploitative extraction.
  leftAnswer: Continuing supplies keeps workers employed and families afloat in the
    short term.
  rightAnswer: Cutting ties ends harm at the source, even if it risks company survival.
